  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/c45c1572-0d0c-41f2-a119-8bc3775e3eb4.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.45347in;height:2.02708in\" /><br />From the diagram,<br />Coordinates of the point <math><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mo>-</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>4</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> (from the line)<br />It must satisfy the equation of the plane</p><p><math><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />So, coordinates of the point <math><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4,9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Point <math> <msup> <mi>B</mi> <mo>′</mo> </msup> </math> must be the foot of perpendicular for point <math><mi>B</mi></math><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Direction ratios of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&gt;</mo></math><br />So, the equation of projection of line is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
